msgstr "⚠ If the video contains <0>real human faces</0>, the AI may reject the job <1>after accepting it</1> — by then compute is already being used, and <2>that charge isn't refunded</2> (tested: it isn't rejected at creation, it only fails partway). Use real-person footage at your own discretion; animation, game footage and blockout previs you shot yourself aren't affected."

